<section class="space-y-6 text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100"><h1 class="text-2xl font-bold">MGS API Documentation</h1><p>MGS API is a software integration platform operated by MGS Technologies Limited. Approved businesses can create verified customers and virtual accounts, receive collections and read their wallet ledger.</p>
<div class="rounded-xl border p-5"><h2 class="font-bold">Authentication</h2><p class="mt-2">Use Authorization: Bearer YOUR_SECRET_KEY. Newly rotated keys support bearer-only authentication. Existing keys also require X-MGS-Public-Key until rotated. Live operations require an approved business and enabled live access. Test keys remain unavailable until provider sandbox isolation is configured.</p><p class="mt-2">Create and rotate keys in API Keys. The secret is displayed once. Optional IP allowlists restrict the source address.</p></div>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead><tr><th class="p-3">Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr v-for="e in endpoints" :key="e.path" class="border-t"><td class="p-3">{{ e.method }}</td><td class="p-3 font-mono">{{ e.path }}</td><td class="p-3">{{ e.purpose }}</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<div class="rounded-xl border p-5"><h2 class="font-bold">Customer KYC</h2><p>POST /api/v1/customers/verify accepts customer_id, type (bvn or nin), and the corresponding 11-digit bvn or nin field. Verification is asynchronous: 202 means queued. Check the customer's KYC status before creating an account. Customer and account writes require X-Idempotency-Key containing 16?255 characters; reuse it only for an identical retry.</p></div>
<div class="rounded-xl border p-5"><h2 class="font-bold">Optional request signing</h2><p>Send X-MGS-Timestamp (Unix seconds) and X-MGS-Signature with the hexadecimal HMAC-SHA256 of the exact raw request body followed by the timestamp, using your bearer secret as the HMAC key. Timestamps expire after five minutes; identical signatures cannot be replayed.</p><p class="mt-2">Existing nonce integrations remain supported: send X-MGS-Nonce and sign timestamp + "." + nonce + "." + raw body using the key's webhook secret. A sha256= prefix is accepted.</p></div>
<div class="rounded-xl border p-5"><h2 class="font-bold">Merchant webhooks</h2><p>Subscribe to payment.success, payment.failed, payout.success, payout.failed and virtual_account.created in Webhooks. Existing collection.success subscriptions remain supported. When both success names are subscribed, payment.success is sent once.</p><p class="mt-2">Validate X-MGS-Signature as sha256= plus HMAC-SHA256(timestamp + "." + exact raw body, your endpoint webhook secret). Enforce timestamp freshness and deduplicate using the event and payment/payout reference. Delivery IDs change for each attempt. Reply with a 2xx status; transient failures retry up to eight attempts. The endpoint secret is separate from the API key signing secret.</p></div>
<div class="rounded-xl border p-5"><h2 class="font-bold">Amounts and responses</h2><p>Submit NGN amounts as decimal strings with at most two fractional digits. Responses include success, data, request_id and pagination meta where applicable. A successful HTTP verification response does not by itself mean payment success: inspect data.status, amount and reference before fulfilment.</p></div>
